gin-bottom:0px\"><u>)</u></a></span><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">,</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">Thanks for your reply. Answers to your questions are inline:</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">1. Does deallocation retain OS settings, such as user configurations and Docker settings?</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">Yes. Deallocation retain OS configurations, settings. Anything on the permanent disk will remain intact after deallocation. Creating single VM using cyclecloud gui, is just like creating VM using azure portal. It is not a cluster and only give benefit of cyclecloud automation</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">2.&nbsp;Does deallocation preserve NVMe data? We understand that NVMe storage is generally ephemeral (volatile), but we noticed that simply rebooting the OS keeps the NVMe data intact.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">Since this is a temporary storage, data from temporary storage MAY not get preserved after deallocation.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">3. Could you please let us know which version you tested with? We are currently using version 8.9.0-3754.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 12pt; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">Today I&nbsp; tested with cyclecloud version 8.9.0-3754, &quot;restart&quot; option using cyclecloud gui is not supported and recommended.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif; font-size:11pt; color:black\"><img id=\"x_image_0\" width=\"602\" height=\"175\" size=\"98715\" data-outlook-trace=\"F:1|T:1\" src=\"cid:image001.png@01DD1F4C.93FC3D60\" data-attachment-id=\"84e36866-4080-4a83-b78c-32179800c3a6\" style=\"width:6.2812in; height:1.8333in; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px\"></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm; font-family:굴림; font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif; color:black\">As far as restart using azure portal, it worked fine for me. The error which you got after restarting using azure portal, will not affect any OS configurations once the VM comes up.<br>Also, restart withi